Spec: TenantInitFromScript

Platform: Rhai script library (vynil-core 0.7.7 engine)

Purpose:
  Seed a `TenantInstance`'s freshly created vitals from an existing restic backup during the very
    first tenant install: render the packaged `init_job.yaml` template into a per-instance init
    Job (a restore Pod running `agent tenant restore` inside the instance namespace, plus its
    ServiceAccount, RoleBinding and optional scripts ConfigMap), apply the documents, and block
    until the Job finishes — all inside the `init_from::run(instance, context)` call made by
    ./install.rhai's first-install gate (`status.vitals` set + `status.tag` unset +
    `spec.initFrom` set). The file itself touches no restic and reads none of the three routing
    fields (source path, snapshot, Secret): @bctx::run(instance, context, `true`) copies them
    verbatim into the rendered pod env (`RESTIC_SNAPSHOT`, `SUB_PATH`, `envs_from` Secret) and
    composes the `RESTIC_TAGS` `tenant:` component; the resolved restore semantics live in the
    dispatched Pod's ./restore.sdd lane, not here. Twin: byte-identical to
    ./../service/init_from.rhai — an actual `diff -u` shows zero hunks — so every tenant delta is
    ambience, four of them: (1) the caller and exit lane are the tenant install script plus
    /agent/src/tenant/install.sdd's exit-1; (2) the marker bridge is @TenantInstance's registered
    `set_status_init_failed`, recording into the tenant-carried `InitFrom` condition; (3) the
    `context` map is built tenant-shaped by ./context.rhai + ./context_tenant.rhai (tenant
    identity under `tenant`, the `namespace` map an alias of it); (4) the rendered Pod dispatches
    the tenant kind (`args` = `tenant` `restore`) into ./restore.sdd, and this is where the
    restore-from-instance, `use_init_from` `true` leg runs for a tenant package.

Exposes:
  @run(@instance, @context) — the module's sole @fn and entry point (`init_from.rhai` + `run`
    match the entry-point patterns of /agent/src/linting/rhai_checker.sdd); reached ONLY through
    @import_run("init_from", instance, context) from ./install.rhai's first-install gate — no Rust
    lane names the module, and the tenant install discards the return value whole
    (./../lib/backup_context.sdd confirms the `true`-leg tenant caller; ./install.sdd the discard).
    A package `scripts/init_from.rhai` shadowing the name replaces this whole lane on that install.

Accepts:
  @instance — the injected @TenantInstance @Dynamic. Direct reads in this file:
    `.metadata.namespace` (Job probe and the apply-namespace argument) and the registered
    @set_status_init_failed method on failure. Everything else flows through collaborators on the
    same object: @bctx::run requires `.status.vitals` (array, unguarded) and `.status.scalables`
    (guarded) — both fields of @TenantInstanceStatus — and, via @use_init_from `true`,
    `spec.initFrom.secretName` / `.subPath` / `.snapshot` each `!= ()`-nullable; `initFrom.version`
    is read by nobody on this path.
  @context — the install-lane map (same object ./install.rhai threads to every bucket), built by
    ./context.rhai over ./../lib/build_context.rhai with the ./context_tenant.rhai additions.
    Direct reads: `template_dir` (unguarded property-on-`()` if non-map — the Rust lane always
    injects it) and `package_dir` (the `${context.package_dir}/pods` gate). The whole map is also
    @bctx::run's data source and the Handlebars render data, so the shipped template reads
    `instance.appslug`, `instance.namespace`, `instance["package"].type`, `cluster.vynil_namespace`,
    `agent_image`, `volumes`/`mounts`/`envs`/`envs_from`/`files`/`has_files`/`service_account` from
    it. Tenant-only keys this lane transports but never reads: `tenant.name` — consumed by
    @bctx::run to append the `,tenant:` tag for `package.type == "tenant"` — and the `namespace`
    map the tenant builder aliases to `tenant` (`ha`, maintenance fields); the key contract is
    owned by ./../lib/build_context.sdd + ./context.sdd + ./context_tenant.sdd and
    ./../lib/backup_context.sdd. Note the map's `instance` key (built view) is NOT the injected
    CR: templates read the key, @bctx::run's CR scans read the argument.
  Hooks — three optional @import_run module names: `init_from_pre`, `init_from_prepare`,
    `init_from_post`, each called with the same (instance, context) pair. None ships in any engine
    directory (./, ./../service, ./../lib) — package `scripts/` slots only.

Returns:
  The `context` map exactly as held after the try/catch, plus an `init_from_post` merge on a map
    return — a value ./install.rhai discards; the lane communicates only by side effects. The
    observable outcomes: the rendered documents applied through @dir::install_obj (shipped
    template yields ServiceAccount `{appslug}-backup`, RoleBinding `{appslug}-backup`, Job
    `{appslug}-init-restore` and — only when `has_files` — ConfigMap `{appslug}-backups-scripts`,
    all without their own `metadata.namespace` so all in `instance.metadata.namespace`), the
    tenant restore landing inside the awaited Pod (`args` render to `tenant` `restore` from
    `instance.package.type`), and the `InitFrom` failure condition on error.

Raises:
  Zero error-fabricating @throw statement: the file's one throw is the bare `throw;` re-throw
    after the failure marker. @import_run swallows only the two skip markers
    (`No ${name} module, skipping.` and `No ${name}::run function, skipping.`), and only those —
    everything else propagates.
  Inside the @try (marker path): a raw raise from @bctx::run (dead/absent `status.vitals`,
    missing `instance` context key, the Cluster-branch Secrets @list_meta read — see its spec's
    Raises), from either @register_partial_dir call on a broken template, from @render_from and
    @yaml_decode_multi, the engine error of a non-map document reaching @dir::install_obj's `kind`
    dot, its `kind: ${obj.kind} is unknown from the apiServer.` throw, or a @wait::all timeout —
    becomes @set_status_init_failed(reason) (verbatim string; non-string through @json_encode)
    then `throw;`: the tenant install aborts with no later bucket and no close, exiting 1
    (/agent/src/tenant/install.sdd), with the condition `InitFrom`/`Warning` `InitFromFail`
    written (/common/src/instance_macros.sdd).
  Outside the @try: @set_status_init_failed's own KubeError replaces the original error; a raise
    inside the `init_from_pre` hook kills the lane with no marker at all; a raise inside the
    `init_from_post` hook (the only statement after the try) likewise leaves no marker even though
    apply+wait already succeeded (twin open points in ./../service/init_from.sdd Tasks).
  The Job-probe inner @try/@catch warn-and-continue: any @k8s_resource, @exist or @list error is
    @log_warn'd (string verbatim, else @json_encode text) and the Job then rides the no-dedup
    apply path; @json_encode of an unserializable payload would re-raise out of that catch into
    the marker path (same open point as ./../lib/backup_context.sdd).

Handles:
  Stock image: all three hook names take the debug-log @import_run skip, the @type_of guard sees
    no map, and the lane runs on the unchanged `context`. A hook returning a non-map leaves the
    previous `context` in force (same merge discipline as ./install.sdd's buckets).
  Idempotent-Job gate: a rendered document whose `kind` is `"Job"` is applied only when no Job of
    that name currently exists in `instance.metadata.namespace` — probe `k8s_resource("Job", ns).@exist()`
    (true once the built-in kind resolved at construction, practically always; false silently
    skips the dedup), then `@list().items` filtered on `metadata.name`. A skipped Job is applied
    nowhere, waited on nowhere, and never logged.
  Documents of every other kind ride no probe: @dir::install_obj always re-applies them.
  Partial precedence: `template_dir` ships first, then `${package_dir}/pods` (only under @is_dir)
    registers second, so a package `pods/init_job.yaml.hbs` / `pods/restore.yaml.hbs` silently
    overwrites the shipped same-name partial — the only supported tenant tweak of the init Pod.
  Failure text shape: the marker reason is the caught engine error's own text — no wrapper, no
    file/line prefix added at this level.

Must:
  Execute exactly: @import_run("init_from_pre") → map-merge guard → @try { @import_run
    ("init_from_prepare") + map-merge → @new_hbs + @register_partial_dir(`context.template_dir`) →
    conditional @register_partial_dir(`${context.package_dir}/pods`) → @yaml_decode_multi of
    @render_from(`"{{> init_job.yaml }}"`, @bctx::run(instance, context, `true`)) → per-document
    Job dedup gate → @dir::install_obj(obj, true, instance.metadata.namespace, false) for every
    applied document → @wait::all(applied_objs, `20*60`) } → on raise: @set_status_init_failed +
    `throw;` → @import_run("init_from_post") + map-merge → return `context`; nothing else, in no
    other order (byte-identical to the service twin's frozen sequence).
  Call @bctx::run with @use_init_from `true` — the ONLY site in the tenant tree that appends env
    `RESTIC_SNAPSHOT` (= `instance.spec.initFrom.snapshot`, possibly `()`-valued per
    ./../lib/backup_context.sdd) and the site that swaps `envs_from` to `initFrom.secretName`
    (default `backup-settings`), redirects `SUB_PATH` to `initFrom.subPath` (default
    `${namespace}/${appslug}` — so by default the tenant restores its own backup path, and a
    different source is addressed purely through `subPath`), and withholds the per-Secret
    `/secrets/` mounts; this file passes all three fields through untouched. As the `true` leg on
    a `tenant` package it is also where the init Pod's `RESTIC_TAGS` gains its `,tenant:` component
    (composition owned by ./../lib/backup_context.sdd).
  Keep the apply posture of ./../lib/install_from_dir.sdd: single-object @install_obj per document
    in decoded-document order, `allow_cluster` `true` (no shipped init document is cluster-scoped;
    the flag is inert today), `force_ns` `false` (documents carry no `metadata.namespace`, so one
    namespace applies: `instance.metadata.namespace` — the tenant instance's own namespace, not
    the tenant-wide namespace list), and NO bucket-ordering pass.
  Await every applied object once, after the whole loop, through one @wait::all(applied_objs,
    `20*60`) call: ConfigMap/ServiceAccount/RoleBinding hit no lane's kind filter, the init Job
    gets `wait_done` 1200 s (contract in ./../lib/wait.sdd) — the whole restore must fit that
    budget or the lane fails via Raises.
  Write the failure marker with the two switched arms as written (string reason verbatim / other
    error `json_encode`d) and re-throw: success is never marked here — no `set_status_*` success
    call, condition or tag; the tenant install close in ./install.sdd stamps `Ready`/`Installed`/
    `tag` later, and its children-variant rebuild evicts the stale `InitFrom` records.
  Emit no @log_info, @log_debug or @log_error line at this level: the only logs are the two
    @log_warn shapes of the Job-probe catch (plus anything the imported collaborators log).
  Keep the import-time surface at the three top-level imports — `"backup_context"` as `bctx`,
    `"install_from_dir"` as `dir`, `"wait"` as `wait`, all side-effect-free per their specs — so
    module load touches no env, filesystem or cluster; a resolver miss is an eval error in the
    install lane before @run starts.
  Resolve every hook name against the four resolver directories frozen by the tenant install Rust
    lane ({package_dir}/scripts first, then {script_dir}/tenant before {script_dir}/lib), so
    packages can ship the three hooks or shadow the whole lane.

Must not:
  Open or close a maintenance/scale window: no `maintenance_start`/`maintenance_stop` @import_run
    here (unlike ./backup.rhai and ./restore.rhai) — during the first install the scalables are
    not applied yet, and any workload quiescing is the restore Pod's own pair (./maintenance_start.rhai
    + ./maintenance_stop.rhai, tenant copies); the maintenance window fields riding in `context`
    are read by nobody on this path.
  Read `spec.initFrom` (or `.status.vitals`) directly — the three routing fields reach the pod
    spec only via @bctx::run, so a second reader would fork the source-selection contract that
    ./../lib/backup_context.sdd owns.
  Wait on, re-apply or mark anything for the deduped existing Job — `to_apply` `false` means the
    object leaves no trace.
  Use the tenant-wide identity surface (`tenant.namespaces`/`tenant.services`) — the install Job,
    its RBAC and the probe all pin to `instance.metadata.namespace` alone; the tenant scope is
    assembled upstream and consumed by the schedule/backup lanes elsewhere.

Depends on:
  ./../lib/backup_context.rhai — @run(..., `true`) half of the env/context contract (spec
    ./../lib/backup_context.sdd, which freezes this file and its service twin as the `true`
    callers; the tenant leg additionally triggers the `,tenant:` tag).
  ./../lib/install_from_dir.rhai — @install_obj single-object apply + applied-entry shape
    (./../lib/install_from_dir.sdd; the applied list here feeds no @remove/diff, only @wait).
  ./../lib/wait.rhai — @wait::all two-arg with the shared `20*60` budget (./../lib/wait.sdd).
  /agent/templates/init_job.yaml.hbs (+ nested /agent/templates/restore.yaml.hbs pod template)
    resolved through `context.template_dir` — the rendered shape itself is template-owned, not
    frozen here.
  vynil-core 0.7.7 engine API — @import_run shim, @new_hbs, @register_partial_dir, @render_from
    (partial-name = filename minus `.hbs`, silent same-name overwrite; /common/src/handlebarshandler.sdd),
    @is_dir, @yaml_decode_multi, @k8s_resource(kind, ns) + @exist, @list, @log_warn, @json_encode,
    @type_of.
  ./../../../common/src/instancetenant.sdd — the `set_status_init_failed` bridge of
    @tenant_rhai_register (@TenantInstance::rhai_set_status_init_failed) and the tenant-carried
    `InitFrom` @ConditionsType stage it patches; /common/src/instance_macros.sdd — the macro body
    behind the condition/event semantics; /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd — the @Script constructor
    mounting all of the above.

References:
  ./install.rhai + ./install.sdd — the sole caller: gate condition, (instance, context) injection
    and the returned-context discard frozen there; /agent/src/tenant/install.sdd — the exit-1 lane
    every raise here lands in.
  ./../service/init_from.sdd — spec of the byte-identical twin source; the four ambience deltas
    are listed in Purpose, everything else the two specs freeze verbatim.
  ./../lib/backup_context.sdd — producer spec, this file named as one of its two `true`-leg
    callers.
  ./restore.rhai + ./restore.sdd and ./backup.rhai + ./backup.sdd — Pod-side siblings:
    ./restore.sdd is the lane the rendered Job dispatches and consumes the env of; both contrast
    CR-side marker posture with their CR-blind throw-only failure surfaces.
  /agent/tests/rhai_backup_redis.rs — the tenant mock harness (never imports `init_from`) and
    /agent/tests/rhai_lifecycle.rs — service dirs only; no test runs this file (Tasks).

Scenario: first tenant install applies and awaits the init job
  Given the tenant install gate true, a context whose `instance.appslug` is `portal`, package type
    `tenant`, `tenant.name` `acme`, no `pods/` dir and no existing `{appslug}-init-restore` Job
  When @run executes
  Then the rendered ServiceAccount, RoleBinding and Job (no ConfigMap when `has_files` is false)
    apply through @dir::install_obj into `instance.metadata.namespace`, the Job Pod spec carries
    `args` `tenant` `restore` and a `RESTIC_TAGS` with the `,tenant:acme` component, @wait::all
    blocks on the Job's completion up to `20*60` seconds, and @run returns `context` — which the
    install gate discards
  No mapped test.

Scenario: restore source rides through untouched
  Given `spec.initFrom` = secretName `peer-creds`, subPath `other-ns/peer`, snapshot `abcd1234`
  When @run renders
  Then the Job pod template carries `envFrom` secret `peer-creds`, `SUB_PATH` `other-ns/peer` and
    `RESTIC_SNAPSHOT` `abcd1234`, and the Pod later runs `agent tenant restore` against them — this
    file never inspects, validates or defaults any of the three
  And with all three absent the defaults apply (Secret `backup-settings`, own-path subPath,
    snapshot `()` per ./../lib/backup_context.sdd)

Scenario: existing init job is skipped and never awaited
  Given a `portal-init-restore` Job still present in the namespace from a failed earlier attempt
  When the rendered Job document reaches the dedup gate
  Then @list finds the name, `to_apply` is `false`, the Job is neither applied nor waited, and
    nothing is logged or marked; the ServiceAccount/RoleBinding still re-apply
  But given the probe itself raises
  Then the error is @log_warn'd and the Job is applied anyway

Tasks:
  [ ] Map the Scenarios to a mapped test file: today none under /agent/tests/ names this module —
      /agent/tests/rhai_lifecycle.rs mounts the service dirs only and
      /agent/tests/rhai_backup_redis.rs proves the tenant mock harness works but imports only the
      backup-prepare/restore modules. Pin the three scenarios with tenant-context and template
      fixtures and a mock Job list.
  [?] Twin-drift watch: the source is `diff`-clean against ./../service/init_from.rhai with zero
      hunks, so any flow fix must now be hand-copied to keep both sources and both specs in
      lockstep — including the silent deduped-Job skip, the hardcoded `20*60` budget and the
      out-of-@try `init_from_post` open points ./../service/init_from.sdd Tasks carries for both
      twins. Decide whether a shared init-lane module in ./../lib taking the kind as a parameter
      replaces the two copies.

Done when:
  Every Scenario carries a passing mock-engine test or a recorded decision, the render→apply→
    wait order and the single marker call still match the source, the `diff` against
    ./../service/init_from.rhai is still empty or the two specs record why it is not, and
    `specdd lint` is green on this file.
